course: dictionary
lesson: 9493
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and steep is one of them. It can describe a slope that rises sharply, a price that is much too high, or a big change. As a verb, it means to soak something in liquid. The context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «You walk a scooter down a steep hill, because you can lose control.» Here steep means a slope that drops sharply. The clues are hill, scooter and lose control. Check by swapping in your meaning: a hill that drops sharply is steep, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Now try a different context: «That's a bit steep!» said about a price. Steep does not mean a slope here. It means the price is much too high. Always ask: does my meaning still fit this sentence?
fact: Steep, steeper and steepest compare how sharp a slope is: a steeper hill is harder to climb than a gentle one.
fact: «Contour lines join points of equal height above sea level, and lines drawn close together mean the ground is steep.»
fact: In maths, a steep line on a graph shows something changing quickly, such as a steep rise in prices.
fact: As a verb, steep means to soak something in liquid, as when you steep tea leaves in hot water.
fact: Common phrases with steep are steep hill, steep slope, steep stairs, steep climb and steep price.
exercise: «Going up the steep hill to school, you click to a bigger back cog.» What does steep mean here? | A price that is much too high | Smooth and flat | Soaked in water | *Rising sharply, like a slope that is hard to climb
exercise: Maya says, «The steep rise in prices surprised everyone.» Which meaning fits? | Soaked in liquid | *A big change, happening quickly | Very quiet | A slope you can climb
exercise: «Steep the tea leaves for three minutes.» What does steep mean as a verb? | To make a price too high | To climb a hill | *To soak in liquid | To hold tightly
test: «That's a bit steep!» said about a price means what? | *A price that is much too high | A small, cheap bargain | Soaked in water | A slope to climb
test: A steep line on a graph shows what? | *Something is changing quickly | The line is the sea | Something is not changing at all | Something has been soaked
exam: «A bucket of water is a pond with steep slippery walls: a small animal that falls in cannot climb out.» What does steep mean here? | Soaked in water | *Rising sharply, so hard to climb | Gentle and sloping | A price that is high
